KEY FACTS from tournament-tiling-explorer.html

TILING MODEL CONVENTION:
  VERTS = [N, N-1, ..., 1]
  Base Hamiltonian path: N->N-1->...->1 (A[k][k+1]=1 for k=0..N-2 in 0-indexed)
  Tiles: for y in 1..N-2: for x in N..y+2 (decreasing): tile (x,y)
  bit=0 [OFF]: arc x->y (lower label loses, x beats y)
  bit=1 [ON]:  arc y->x (higher label loses, y beats x = "backward")

  TRANS_MAP: tile (x,y) <-> tile (N-y+1, N-x+1)
  Self-paired tiles: those where (N-y+1,N-x+1)=(x,y), i.e., x+y=N+1
  Grid-symmetric: bits[i]==bits[TRANS_MAP[i]] for all non-self-paired tiles

  Blue flip-line: {T, T_flip} where T_flip=all-bits-inverted, BOTH grid-sym
  Black flip-line: BOTH not grid-sym (symmetry is preserved by tile complement)

